{"title":"Subtraction","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Subtraction</b> is the mathematical <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Operation\" title=\"Operation\">operation</a> which combines two quantities.  The minus sign, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add22d9bda21e86390bc74fa4dde17730a442da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, is used to indicate subtraction. Subtraction is the inverse of addition:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9ba5c78cc306152a2b1d005c488cd4d7c9445e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b=a+(-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Subtraction&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic\" title=\"Arithmetic\">Arithmetic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">Number theory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Addition\" title=\"Addition\">Addition</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiplication\" title=\"Multiplication\">Multiplication</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Division\" title=\"Division\">Division</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Counting\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Counting\">Counting</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Subtraction&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204636\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU ti